#, fuzzy
msgid "The fix was faithfully reusing the chunks — but each one was 4x oversized. 90 MB of old gen wasted on empty space. With the fix, old gen after Full GC sits at ~728 MB vs ~713 MB without it — less headroom on a 910 MB old gen, *causing the throughput regression*."
msgstr "修复方案是忠实地复用这些块——但每个块的大小都超出了实际需求的4倍。90 MB的老代内存被浪费在空闲空间上。 采用该修复方案后，完整垃圾回收（Full GC）后的旧代内存占用约为 728 MB，而未采用时约为 713 MB——在 910 MB 的旧代内存中，可用空间更少， *从而导致吞吐量下降* 。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Interestingly, *the actual stack size used at freeze was ~1,100 words during warmup but dropped to ~286 words during steady state* — even though the application code hadn't changed. The chunks were right-sized _when they were born_, but the demand shrank over time while the capacity stayed frozen."
msgstr "有趣的是 *，在预热阶段，实际使用的栈大小约为 1,100 个字，但在稳态期间却降至约 286 个字* ——尽管应用程序代码并未发生变化。这些数据块 _在创建时_ 大小恰到好处，但随着时间的推移，需求逐渐减少，而容量却保持不变。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "What happened between warmup and steady state that made the same code need 4x less stack?"
msgstr "在预热阶段和稳态阶段之间发生了什么，导致相同的代码所需的栈空间减少了4倍？"

#, fuzzy
msgid "The Root Cause: JIT Compilation Timing"
msgstr "根本原因：JIT 编译时机"

#, fuzzy
msgid "The answer is https://dev.java/learn/jvm/tool/compiler/[tiered compilation]."
msgstr "答案是 link:https://dev.java/learn/jvm/tool/compiler/[分层编译] 。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "The JVM compiles Java methods in tiers. *C1* is the fast first-tier compiler — it produces correct code quickly but doesn't optimize aggressively. *C2* is the optimizing compiler — it kicks in later for hot methods and produces much more compact code. Our data shows that *C2-compiled code produces a significantly smaller frozen stack than C1-compiled code*."
msgstr "JVM 采用分层方式编译 Java 方法。 *C1* 是快速的第一层编译器——它能快速生成正确的代码，但不会进行激进的优化。 *C2* 是优化编译器——它会在稍后针对热方法启动，并生成更加紧凑的代码。 我们的数据显示 *，与 C1 编译的代码相比，C2 编译的代码产生的冻结栈要小得多* 。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "We proved this with a control experiment: `-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1` forces the JVM to use only C1 (no C2)."
msgstr "我们通过一项对照实验证明了这一点： `-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1` 会强制 JVM 仅使用 C1（不使用 C2）。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Normal (C1 + C2)"
msgstr "正常 (C1 + C2)"

#, fuzzy
msgid "C1 only"
msgstr "仅限C1"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Chunk capacity"
msgstr "块容量"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*1,149 words*"
msgstr "*1,149个词*"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*1,144 words*"
msgstr "*1,144个单词*"

#, fuzzy
msgid "With C1-only, the chunk capacity matches what we see in the pooled run under normal compilation. *The ~1,149-word chunks are C1-sized.* Under normal compilation, C2 shrinks the frozen stack to ~280 words — but the shared VT pool is created during warmup, before C2 kicks in. Its VTs are born with C1-sized chunks, and *that capacity is locked in forever.*"
msgstr "在仅启用 C1 的情况下，块容量与正常编译下池化运行中观察到的结果一致。 *这些约1,149字的块大小与C1一致。* 在正常编译下，C2会将冻结栈缩小至约280字——但共享的VT池是在预热阶段创建的，即在C2生效之前。其VT在创建时就带有C1大小的块，且 *该容量将永久锁定。*"

#, fuzzy
msgid "The reuse fix keeps those bloated chunks alive in old gen — forever — leaving the garbage collector to fight over the scraps of a heap it can never fully reclaim."
msgstr "“重用修复”机制会让这些臃肿的块在旧代中永远存活下去，导致垃圾回收器只能在堆中争夺那些残渣，却永远无法完全回收该堆。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "So&#8230;&#8203; Don&#8217;t Pool?"
msgstr "那么……​ 不要凑钱？"

#, fuzzy
msgid "It depends. With small heaps, clearly not. In production, you don't control VT lifecycles — and with a shared pool, you can't predict which code path a VT will be used for, whether that code is warm, hot, or never compiled by C2. Too aggressive caching risks bloating the runtime heap forever."
msgstr "这要视情况而定。对于较小的堆而言，显然不是这样。在生产环境中，你无法控制虚拟目标（VT）的生命周期——而且在共享池中，你无法预测某个虚拟目标会被用于哪个代码路径，也无法判断该代码是“温”的、还是“热”的，抑或从未被 C2 编译过。缓存策略过于激进，可能会导致运行时堆永久性膨胀。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "But in Quarkus, we're experimenting with different options to improve our Loom integration — boldly going where no one has gone before. That means running with scissors that everyone told us are too sharp. We do it for the sake of innovation, and because we now know _why_ they cut. As the saying goes, *the journey matters more than the destination.*"
msgstr "但在 Quarkus，我们正在尝试各种方案来改进与 Loom 的集成——大胆地踏入前人未至之境。这就像拿着一把大家都说太锋利的剪刀奔跑。我们之所以这样做，既是为了创新，也是因为我们现在已经明白它 _为何会_ 割伤人。正如俗话所说， *过程比结果更重要。*"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Takeaways"
msgstr "要点"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*Pooling VTs doesn't save what you think it saves.* Under the hood, the JVM can still allocate new StackChunks — the biggest cost you were trying to avoid."
msgstr "*合并 VT 并不能节省你想象中的开销。* 在底层，JVM 仍然会分配新的 StackChunk—— *而这* 正是你原本试图避免的最大开销。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*The \"don't pool\" advice is broadly sensible.*"
msgstr "*“不要聚在一起”这一建议总体上是合理的。*"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*Fixing one problem can create a worse one.* Eliminating allocation churn sounds great until you realize you're pinning oversized objects in old gen forever."
msgstr "*解决一个问题可能会引发更严重的问题。* 消除内存分配波动听起来很不错，直到你意识到自己正在将超大对象永久地锁定在旧代中。"

#, fuzzy
msgid "*Shared pools are unpredictable.* You can't control when VTs are born, what code they'll run, or how the JIT has compiled it. That unpredictability is the real danger."
msgstr "*共享池具有不可预测性。* 你无法控制虚拟机（VT）何时生成、它们将运行什么代码，以及JIT编译器是如何编译这些代码的。这种不可预测性才是真正的危险所在。"

